.nf
YASMV manual                                                 check-property

.ti 0
SYNOPSIS

.in 3
check-property <name> -depth <N> [options]

.ti 0
DESCRIPTION

.fi
.in 3
Search for a counterexample to a saved safety property through depth N
(0 to 10000 transitions). Requires a loaded model and a property saved with
property set. A counterexample is replayed and selected in the native trace
register. A property that holds through this bound is not an unbounded proof.

-c <expression> adds an assumption (repeatable). -wall-ms <N> limits computation
time; -conflicts <N> and -propagations <N> limit solver work. -async submits a
background job. Use job wait to retrieve its result or job cancel to cancel it.
Ctrl-C cancels a waiting job. job show -full displays complete evidence.
Shell options use one dash; -- starts an SMV comment.

.ti 0
EXAMPLES

.nf
.in 3
>> property set once !DUPLICATE
>> check-property once -depth 12
>> dump-trace

.ti 0
SEE ALSO

.fi
.in 3
help property, help prove-property, help job, help dump-trace.
